"attrs": {}, "children": ["The external unit recovers the Manchester-coded backscatter signal and decrypts the payload. Uplink activity is enabled by an authenticated downlink request."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=181", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 5.11 · p. 165 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "aside", "attrs": {"class": "evidence-note"}, "children": [{"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["What the prototype demonstrates"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The silicon validates the wireless power infrastructure and credential-gated telemetry. During link measurements, TRNG-derived credentials and keys were supplied from external microcontroller EEPROM because the intended on-chip antifuse memory was unreliable. XOR-based packet protection and dual-credential checks are the implemented mechanisms; this is not a claim of independently certified security or a complete clinical implant. Recording/stimulation integration, reliable embedded credential retention and implant-scale packaging remain next steps."]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "related"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["CONTINUE EXPLORING"]}, {"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Explore the RF and security circuits"]}]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/rf-energy"}, "children": ["RF energy harvesting & PMU ↗"]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/neurolock"}, "children": ["NeuroLock & hardware security ↗"]}]}]}]}